import * as THREE from "three";

/**
 * The Raccoon primitive's mesh, baked into the source.
 *
 * It ships as data rather than as a file under public/ for the same reason
 * the other primitives do: a primitive has to exist the moment the node is
 * dropped on the canvas, with no loader, no path to rehydrate and nothing to
 * go missing. The OBJ loader nodes stay the way to bring in *your own*
 * models — rehydrateFiles is Tauri-only and reads absolute local paths, so
 * anything shipped with the app cannot go through them.
 *
 * Stored base64 rather than as number literals: the same 33,600 floats spelt
 * out as an array is a ~215KB literal for the TypeScript parser to chew on
 * every build, against ~176KB of string it never looks inside.
 *
 * Geometry is non-indexed — the source OBJ gives every triangle corner its
 * own normal and UV, so all 4,200 corners are already unique and an index
 * buffer would only add 4,200 more numbers to say so. Centred on X/Z with
 * its feet left on y=0, so it stands on the ground plane and turns about
 * itself.
 */

